id: MONDO:0017926
name: Pacak-Zhuang syndrome
def: "A neoplastic syndrome caused by early postzygotic mosaic gain-of-function mutations in EPAS1 (encoding hypoxia-inducible factor 2 alpha, HIF-2 alpha), characterized by multiple paragangliomas, somatostatinomas, and polycythemia, and variably associated with vascular malformations and neural tube defects." [PMID:37450881]
